  "articleSummary": "The article argues that search is not a single problem and that semantic/vector search should complement—not replace—exact-match, lexical, and fuzzy search in a hybrid architecture. It explains embeddings, vectors, semantic relevance, and technologies such as pgvector, Qdrant, Weaviate, Pinecone, Milvus, Elasticsearch, and other vector-search systems, comparing their deployment models, licensing, capabilities, and workload fit. The tone is an analytical, practical tutorial aimed at engineers making search-architecture decisions, emphasizing tool selection and clear technical reasoning rather than “embed everything.” A recurring framing device contrasts deterministic lookups like finding an email address with open-ended relevance searches such as finding debugging advice.",
